Legend: `!` after a field name = required (from the app's base view) —
a step form that writes such a field must not submit it empty.
A lookup field lists its keys after the type (`[lookup/select: a|b|c]`);
these are the ONLY valid write values — quote them into the brief verbatim,
the matching labels come from LOOKUP_OPTIONS at runtime.
`⚙` lists the service methods for that entity, spelled exactly.
`✚` lists the entity's Enriched* fields and its enrich() signature,
spelled exactly — quote both verbatim; an invented enriched field or
a missing map is a guaranteed type error.

Modules — copy these paths verbatim into a subagent brief:
  @/types/app                            entity types, APP_IDS, LOOKUP_OPTIONS
  @/types/enriched                       EnrichedMitgliedsbeitraege, EnrichedVeranstaltungen — the COMPLETE list, no other Enriched* type exists
  @/lib/enrich                           the enrich functions — exact fields and signatures on the `✚` line of each entity below; every listed map is REQUIRED, and no other enriched field exists
  @/services/livingAppsService           LivingAppsService, createRecordUrl, extractRecordId
  @/hooks/useDashboardData               useDashboardData — the RAW arrays (one per entity, camelCase), their setters, loading, error, fetchAll + mitgliederMap, raeumeMap; it carries NO enriched arrays — build those with the `✚` call below
  @/lib/formatters                       lookupKey, formatDate
  @/components/blocks/IntentWizardShell  IntentWizardShell
